  ## 4. Chat bubble widget

  `lib/features/chat/presentation/widgets/chat_bubble.dart` (240 lines).

  - Constructor (line 22-24): `ChatBubble({required this.message, this.onRetry, super.key})` — only 2 optional/required params today, `message: ChatUiMessage` and `onRetry: VoidCallback?`.
  - `isUser` computed at line 81: `final isUser = message.role == ChatMessageRole.user;` — this is exactly the flag a new `onBookmark`/bookmark-icon should gate on, since the prototype doc says bookmark only applies to **user** messages ("Bookmark on each user message...").
  - `onRetry` is rendered conditionally only `if (message.status == ChatMessageStatus.failed)` (line 212-213), as a tappable `InkWell` wrapped in `Semantics(button: true, ...)` only when the callback is non-null (lines 104-131) — same conditional-Semantics pattern a bookmark affordance should reuse.
  - The bubble's layout is a `Column` (lines 161-216): bubble `Container` (text), `SizedBox` gap, optional retry indicator, `timeCaption`. A bookmark icon/button would most naturally go either inside the bubble `Container`'s row (next to or below content) or as a new row alongside `timeCaption` — no existing slot reserved for it; this is a layout decision for the spec, not yet present in code.
  - No bookmark-related code exists anywhere in `chat_bubble.dart` currently.

  **Design tokens available** (`lib/core/design_tokens.dart`):
  - No literal "ochre" named token exists. The ochre-ish color is `colorAccent = Color(0xFFC98A3E)` (line 27) — doc comment at line 26 literally says "CTA, insight, **saved bookmark**." `colorWarningSync` (line 57) is the exact same hex `0xFFC98A3E` — also ochre, used today for the sync-badge "Sincronizando" dot.
  - `colorError = Color(0xFFB3402A)` (line 51) — used today for the chat retry indicator text (`chat_bubble.dart:117`) and would double as the bookmark "error" sub-state's red warning color.
  - `colorSuccess = Color(0xFF4C6B4F)` (line 54) — green, used for `SyncBadgeSynchronized`.
  - No centralized icon-token constants exist (confirmed by grep) — icons in this codebase are inline `Icons.xxx` (Material) literals chosen ad hoc at each call site (e.g. `Icons.backspace_outlined`, design_tokens.dart:481 comment), only **sizes** are tokenized (`dialogIconSize` etc., lines 265-283). There is no existing spinner/check/warning *icon* token — a bookmark button implementing idle/saving/saved/error sub-states (per `docs/input/prototype/prototype-extract.md:67`: "idle, saving (spinner), saved (ochre check), error (red warning)") would need to pick its own Material icons (e.g. `CircularProgressIndicator`-style spinner for "saving", `Icons.check`/similar for "saved", `Icons.warning`/similar for "error") — nothing pre-built to reuse, consistent with how `chat_bubble.dart`'s own cursor/retry treatments are hand-built widgets, not token-driven icon widgets.
