  /// call it fire-and-forget (without awaiting).
  typedef IsolatedSideEffect<T> = Future<Either<Failure, T>> Function(
    Future<T> Function() action,
  );

  /// Placeholder implementation — throws until RF10 replaces it.
  Future<Either<Failure, T>> isolatedSideEffect<T>(
    Future<T> Function() action,
  ) {
    throw UnimplementedError(
      'isolatedSideEffect is a typed stub (AD-13) — implemented in RF10.',
    );
  }
  ```
  This is a **typed stub that currently throws `UnimplementedError`** — the real implementation is explicitly deferred to "RF10," and the file's own doc comment names RF10 (chat/bookmark, matching Story 6.4) as its "first consumer." This confirms: Story 6.4 is expected to *replace* the stub body of `isolatedSideEffect()` with a real implementation (presumably `try`/`catch` wrapping `action()` and converting any thrown exception into `Left(Failure.malformedResponse(...))` or similar — exact mapping not specified anywhere in code, spec must decide), not create the file from scratch. No test file for it exists yet (`find test/core -iname "*isolated*"` → empty).

